---
/**
 * BucketsSection — "The Three Buckets" section (Figma node 176:20).
 *
 * Top: pull-quote left + "Four rules that make this work" right.
 * Then: shared BucketGraphic with the animated three-bucket cascade.
 *
 * Used on /fill-the-first-bucket.
 */
import BucketGraphic from '~/components/ui/BucketGraphic.astro';
---

<section class="not-prose w-full py-12 md:py-16 lg:py-[80px]">
  <div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-container flex-col gap-12 px-5 sm:px-8 md:gap-16 md:px-16 lg:px-[120px]">
    {/* ── TOP: pull-quote | rules ── */}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-10 lg:flex-row lg:items-start lg:gap-[120px]">
      {/* Pull quote */}
      <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-[1.3em] font-heading text-h3 font-normal leading-[1.2] text-heading">
        <p>
          The price goes up as the evidence goes down. Bucket one is free and it is the one that matters most.{' '}
          <span class="text-accent">Bucket three costs thousands and may do nothing at all.</span>
        </p>
        <p>Almost nobody in this business will tell you that, because most of them sell bucket three.</p>
      </div>

      {/* Four rules */}
      <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-6">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-h2 font-normal leading-none text-heading">
          Four rules that make<br class="hidden sm:block" /> this work.
        </h2>
        <div class="font-sans text-small leading-[1.3] text-muted space-y-[1.3em]">
          <p>
            <strong class="font-bold">1. Overflow, not completion.</strong>{' '}
            You never &ldquo;finish&rdquo; a bucket. You fill it as well as you reasonably can, and what spills over (spare
            money, spare attention, spare Tuesdays) runs down to the next. Nobody is being told to wait.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-bold">2. Inside bucket one there is no order. </strong>
            The buckets are a sequence; the four basics inside bucket one are not. Show up for any one, stay for all four.
            Start with whichever you can face on a Tuesday.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-bold">3. The buckets refill.</strong>{' '}
            Bucket one is a permanent habit, not a phase you graduate from. You do not stop walking because you have moved
            on to blood tests.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-bold">4. We are not against bucket three. </strong>
            Recreational anti-aging is fine. If you enjoy it and can afford it, help yourself, the same as a weekend in Las
            Vegas. The objection is buying bucket three while bucket one sits empty.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* ── Shared bucket graphic — full width here so it does not feel cramped ── */}
    <div class="w-full">
      <BucketGraphic />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
